\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Convention}
\title{Training and evaluation laws}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{We write #{\mathcal Q_{\mathrm{tr}}} for the law that supplies training
tasks and #{\mathcal Q_{\mathrm{ev}}} for the law used to report capability.
The two laws may be equal, but equality is an experimental assumption rather
than a notation convention.}

\p{This is an FTIP convention. Chapter 3 of
\citef{sutton2018reinforcement} makes the environment law part of policy
evaluation. Sections 3--4 of \citef{yue2025does} compare post-trained and
base policies on held-out reasoning evaluations. Neither source requires the
two laws above to differ; FTIP records the choice explicitly.}

\p{Any data-dependent choice of #{\mathcal Q_{\mathrm{ev}}}, its examples, or
its metric must be recorded. Otherwise the reported evaluation is no longer
independent of the training protocol.}
